                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Shantae: Risky's Revenge is a charming little metroidvania with colorful visuals, catchy music, and a protagonist whose hair is apparently a perfectly viable weapon. Who needs swords when you can weaponize your ponytail?\n\nExploration is fun, the transformations add some variety, and the game's humor gives it plenty of personality. Unfortunately, the world can feel a bit small, and the backtracking occasionally gets tedious, especially when you're trying to remember where that one ability you just unlocked is actually useful.\n\nStill, it's a delightful adventure with plenty of charm packed into a relatively small package.",
